2026-10-26 — Add fixed token lifetime and inactivity logout

The local demo issuer now issues 30-minute JWTs. Both the enterprise and local JWT decoders require `iat` and `exp`, reject tokens whose declared lifetime exceeds 30 minutes, and reject tokens at their exact expiration or 30-minute age on every authenticated request. The authenticated frontend shell signs users out after 10 minutes without mouse, pointer/click, keyboard, scroll, or touch activity; interaction never changes the token deadline. Idle activity and logout signals are shared between tabs, the current token is cached rather than refreshed by the app, and 401 responses clear the client session and redirect to login with a reason notice.

