2026-10-14 — Added safe Form Master lifecycle actions and immutable mapping snapshots

Implementation: Form Master now provides a responsive row actions dialog for Duplicate, Rename, Remap, Delete permanently, Activate/Deactivate, and View Published Version, while retaining Edit Draft and New Version. All management routes use the existing validated tenant resolver and `ADMINISTER_ORGANIZATION` permission. Duplicate creates a separate form and draft transactionally; the current published version is the default source and an explicit source version may be selected. Draft selection is never implicit. Rename preserves published version names; remapping writes the new mapping into a draft snapshot, while the existing published version keeps its original mapping until a replacement is published. The Remap dialog reads active-area purpose/stage choices from `GET /api/v1/configuration/form-mappings`, which filters them through backend mapping rules. Deactivation checks active workflow coverage against the actual published version snapshot. Permanent deletion removes only never-published, unused drafts, rejects protected history with HTTP 409, and writes an independent append-only audit snapshot.

