2026-10-24 — Make defect detail reads consistent across permitted entry points

The aircraft Defect List intentionally exposes active tenant cases to Reviewer, Maintenance, and organization-administrator users, while the generic detail API previously required a Reviewer-team route or active Maintenance assignment. A case visible in that list could therefore open as “Defect unavailable.” The generic detail endpoint now follows the same read-only tenant visibility as the aircraft list for non-Reporter-scoped readers; report-only users remain limited to their own cases unless they separately have `DEFECT_VIEW_ALL`. The aircraft-specific detail route remains bound to both tenant and selected aircraft and keeps its Reporter ownership check, as required by the aircraft-list policy. The Defect Log Book list query and all workflow mutation checks are unchanged; viewing a detail does not grant a Reviewer decision, Maintenance action, reassignment, verification, or closure permission.

