2026-10-24 — Add per-field combined upload limits for IMAGE_UPLOAD and FILE_UPLOAD

Report Master now configures a Total upload size (MB) independently from Max file size (MB), and the Dynamic Forms renderer shows the configured total and current combined selection. New upload fields default to 20 MiB per file, 1–3 files, and 30 MiB total. Existing version JSON without a total setting retains its former maximum envelope (`maxFileSizeBytes × maxCount`); no form-definition database column was needed. Limits use binary megabytes (1 MiB = 1,048,576 bytes).

Both image and general file fields validate allowed extension/MIME/content as before, the individual limit, count, and combined bytes. The browser recalculates totals when items are selected or removed; a new batch that exceeds count or combined size is rejected as a batch while the existing selection remains. The backend repeats the checks against trusted stored sizes, validates same-field attachment IDs together at submission, serializes pending uploads per defect, rejects multi-file multipart requests, and cleans up the object if metadata/audit persistence fails. The existing bounded 64 MB multipart request ceiling remains; the maximum individual multipart file size is now 20 MB. The new database check permits attachment rows up to 20 MiB.

